# =============================================================================
# ClinIQ — .gitignore
# =============================================================================
# This file tells git which files to leave OUT of the repository. The groups
# below are ordered by importance:
#   1. SECRETS   — keys and passwords (never push)
#   2. PATIENT-DERIVED DATA — MIMIC-III is licensed; never push
#   3. Model files that are generated or too large
#   4. Everything else that is regenerated (caches, builds, logs, editor files)
#
# Paths are relative to this folder (icu_monitor/).
# To check why a file is or is not ignored:   git check-ignore -v <path>
# =============================================================================


# =============================================================================
# 1. SECRETS — NEVER PUSH THESE
# =============================================================================
# .env holds the real GROQ_API_KEY. Anyone with the key can use your Groq
# account. The template .env.example is meant to be committed (it holds only a
# placeholder), so it is explicitly allowed again below.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Streamlit secrets (may contain API keys or database URLs).
# .streamlit/config.toml is intentionally NOT ignored (theme + server settings).
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Google Cloud credential files (used for BigQuery in train_federated.py Phase 0).
# `gcloud auth application-default login` stores credentials outside the project,
# but these patterns stop an exported key file from being committed by accident.
*service-account*.json
*credentials*.json
application_default_credentials.json


# =============================================================================
# 2. PATIENT-DERIVED DATA — MIMIC-III IS LICENSED, NEVER PUSH
# =============================================================================
# The training data comes from MIMIC-III (PhysioNet). The data-use agreement
# allows only credentialed users to hold it, so anything built from it stays off
# GitHub, even though it is de-identified. Share it only with other credentialed
# people, privately.
# Source: BigQuery  mimic-project-2.dataset_v2  (rebuilt; see docs/SQL_COMMANDS.md)

# The SQLite database: the 41,798-row fl_training table (MIMIC-derived) plus the
# live vitals and prediction history. About 56 MB.
# Recreate the demo tables with:  python migrate_to_db.py
# Recreate fl_training with:      python train_federated.py  (needs BigQuery access)
models/icu_monitor.db
models/icu_monitor.db-shm
models/icu_monitor.db-wal
models/icu_monitor.db-journal

# The held-out test set (10,450 scaled ICU stays, ~4.5 MB), written by
# train_federated.py Phase 0. It is built from MIMIC-III rows, so it is not pushed.
# If it is missing, a later training run warns and falls back to a split of the
# hospitals' own data (results then look better than they really are).
models/fl_test_X.npy
models/fl_test_y.npy

# Exports and hand-off packages made to share the dataset with another
# credentialed person (zips, parquet or CSV dumps of the training tables).
# These contain MIMIC-derived rows and must never be pushed.
handoff*/
handoff*.zip
*.zip
*.parquet
data/fl_training/

# Legacy CSV backups from before the app moved to SQLite. The canonical data is
# in models/icu_monitor.db. The folders no longer exist; the rules stay in case
# old copies reappear.
models/patient_vitals/*.csv
models/prediction_history/*.csv
!models/patient_vitals/.gitkeep
!models/prediction_history/.gitkeep


# =============================================================================
# 3. MODEL FILES — what is and is not committed
# =============================================================================
# COMMITTED (needed to run the dashboard without retraining):
#   models/federated_model.pth     the trained network (~0.3 MB)
#   models/scaler.pkl              StandardScaler for the 108 inputs
#   models/tfidf_vectorizer.pkl    TF-IDF with the 90-word SOFA list
#   models/feature_columns.pkl     the 108 input names in order
#   models/shap_background.npy     300 background rows for SHAP (~0.1 MB)
#   models/training_metadata.json  settings + results; the SOFA validation drawer reads it
#
# NOT committed:
# Intermediate checkpoints saved during real federated training (server.py writes
# federated_model_latest.pth every round; federated_model.pth is the best round and
# is the one that matters). "best" is an older name, kept in case it reappears.
models/federated_model_latest.pth
models/federated_model_best.pth

# The browser camera monitor downloads this ~12 MB MediaPipe face model itself.
# Ignored in case a copy is saved into the project.
face_landmarker.task


# =============================================================================
# 4. REGENERATED FILES
# =============================================================================

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
*.egg-info/
*.egg
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ── Virtual environments ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# python setup.py creates venv/ in this folder.
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Federated-learning run output (Ray / Flower) ─────────────────────────────
# Ray writes session folders while the simulation runs; they are large and
# useless to others (they normally live in /tmp/ray).
ray_results/
.ray/

# ── Test and coverage reports ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Made by: pytest --cov, Vitest coverage, Playwright
.coverage
coverage.xml
coverage/
htmlcov/
test-results/
playwright-report/
playwright/.cache/

# ── Frontend (React + Vite) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Installed by `npm install` / produced by `npm run build`.
frontend/dist/
frontend/node_modules/

# The frontend tests live in tests/ (outside frontend/), so Vitest needs this
# symlink to find the packages:   ln -s frontend/node_modules node_modules
# It is written WITHOUT a trailing slash on purpose: a pattern "node_modules/"
# matches only real folders, so a symlink would NOT be ignored and could be
# committed by accident (checked with `git check-ignore`).
node_modules

# Auto-generated by the Vite template; the project uses its own oxlint settings.
frontend/.oxlintrc.json

# ── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Includes training output saved from the terminal, such as train_run.log.
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ── Jupyter ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── macOS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Icon?

# ── Windows ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# ── Editors and IDEs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only the personal VS Code settings are ignored; shared settings can still be committed.
.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
